# Course Slides (Reveal.js)

Self-contained HTML decks served at `/course-slides/{slug}/`. Output: `public/course-slides/{slug}/index.html`.

## Workflow

1. Resolve course by slug, title, or `/admin/courses/{id}`.
2. Load data via `sql` from `@/lib/db` (fields in `app/(public)/education/[slug]/page.tsx`).
3. Start from `.cursor/skills/course-slides/reveal-template.html`.
4. Replace `{{PLACEHOLDERS}}` and inject `<section>` blocks inside `<div class="slides">`.

## Content rules

- **12–20 slides**, Spanish (es-AR), built from DB fields only.
- Structure: title → agenda → short description → learning objective → one slide per outcome → logistics → notes (if any) → closing.
- Parse outcomes: `learningOutcomes.split('\n').filter(line => line.trim())`.
- Labels: `COURSE_LEVELS`, `COURSE_MODALITIES` from `@/lib/consts/course-consts`.
- Stay faithful to outcome text; do not invent topics. If thin, add facilitation slides (ejercicio, discusión), not fabricated technical detail.

## HTML rules

- Reveal.js via CDN only — no npm, no build step.
- Branding: `#0f172a` background, `#2563eb` accents, logo `/pelambres_logo.svg`.
- One `<section>` per slide. Optional `<aside class="notes">` for speaker notes.
- On regenerate, preserve content inside `<!-- MANUAL:START -->` … `<!-- MANUAL:END -->` blocks.

## Verify

- Path slug matches DB `slug`; every outcome has a slide; no empty `<section>` elements.
